From f2bf3394098a5380fd6b35fd98fc14e044f4d0ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Domack <patrickdk77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 19:38:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec, avformat: add Olympus DS2 decoder and demuxer

Add support for the Olympus Digital Speech Standard Pro (DS2) audio
format used by Olympus DS-, DM-, and DPM-series dictation recorders.

The DS2 codec is a CELP variant with two modes:
  - SP (Standard Play): 12000 Hz, 14 reflection coefficients
  - QP (Quality Play):  16000 Hz, 16 reflection coefficients

This patch is complementary to the existing DSS support in FFmpeg
(libavcodec/dss_sp.c and libavformat/dss.c by Oleksij Rempel, 2014).
The two formats share a similar 0x600 header layout but use different
codebooks and frame structures; the demuxer added here only accepts
the DS2 magic (\x03ds2), so DSS files continue to route to the
existing dss_sp decoder.

Validation against the Hirpara reference Rust decoder: SNR 66.4 dB on
a 37s test sample; +/-1 LSB rounding noise is the entire delta
(591360 samples compared; 99.98% differ by at most one quantization
step, 1 sample by 3, max).

Closes Trac ticket #6091.

Based on a codec specification reverse-engineered from the Olympus
DLLs (DssDecoder.dll, dss32.dll) via Ghidra by Kieran Hirpara
(https://github.com/hirparak/dss-codec, MIT, 2026). The CELP
algorithm in libavcodec/ds2.c was implemented from the specification
text in FFmpeg trac #6091 by Patrick Domack; the numerical
quantization tables (reflection codebooks, pitch and excitation
gains, pulse amplitudes) are sourced from Hirpara's reference
implementation, which originally extracted them from the Olympus
codebooks via Ghidra. Both the algorithm and the tables are
MIT-licensed.

Patrick Domack relicensed his contribution under MIT / public-domain
terms explicitly for upstream FFmpeg merge, see:
https://github.com/hirparak/dss-codec/issues/1

Signed-off-by: Guillain d'Erceville <guillain@poulpe.us>
